  "term": "isocarboxazid",
  "definition": "Isocarboxazid is an antidepressant that works by blocking monoamine oxidase, an enzyme that breaks down brain chemicals such as norepinephrine and serotonin. By raising levels of these mood-related neurotransmitters, it can affect mood and emotions.",
